    "input_requirements": [
      "Matthew's wavelet inputs require the complete recording, including future samples. This is retrospective classification; a target day's raw signal alone is insufficient.",
      "LA change is next-day minus current-day circadian amplitude. Recording day 13 has a missing LA change to avoid the final buffer's endpoint-sensitive amplitude; the model fills this using a median learned from its fitting data. All target days remain included.",
      "Matthew's 37.2 \u00b0C and 15 counts/minute thresholds were chosen during development exploration and frozen before this run. Validation scores after feature design are exploratory.",
      "Vivian's activity-adjusted CBT inputs use per-mouse cleaning and activity regression over the complete recording; wavelet inputs also include future samples and buffers. They support retrospective classification, not isolated-day prediction. Extraction uses no labels or other mice; the shared export is uncentered.",
      "Alisha's DTW inputs compare each day with the same mouse's other 13 recording days, including future days and buffers 1 and 14. They require the complete 14-day recording for retrospective classification; an isolated day's signal is insufficient. These comparisons use no labels or other mice.",
      "LA\u2013CBT relationship features describe a complete target day's paired signals using five-minute bins and within-day ten-minute changes. They use no labels, other days, other mice, or fitted population quantities. Within-day forward changes require end-of-day retrospective access; the complete combined model still requires the original contributors' full-recording inputs.",
      "These are observational descriptors inspired by Burks and Smarr (2026), not their fitted dynamical coefficients, causal heating/cooling estimates, hormonal residuals, or a reproduction of their forecasting model. Hours 6\u201312 remain elapsed recording-day hours; light/clock alignment is unconfirmed."
    ]
